Z||000002||dman||05-04-2000||10:54 PM||||I'm in Southern California. And I just got off the phone with the owner. The car is in San Juan Capistrano. The owner seems like a good guy. From what he described, this car sounds pretty darn sweet.<P>He did the conversion back in 97. Though it has about 56k original miles on the car, the engine only has about 1200 miles on it. It has drop forged pistons in it (the old stock ones were destroyed due to detonation).<P>The turbo install was performed by the owner. He custom fabricated stainless steel 304 pipe to mate with the stock exhaust manifold to the turbo. The intercooler mounts in a custom rear decklid hoodscoop. This car has complete instrumentation (all the gauges you need and should have). He tells me that he has two programs for the computer (street use and race use?).<P>It has NOS hookups (hidden in the deep well of the trunk).<P>For the price he is asking, this car sounds like a deal.<P>I'd be very interested in this car for myself but I've got too many project cars right now. However after talking with the owner about all of the cool mods on this car I'm so tempted! Oh well...we'll see.||||reg||1
